1:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A butt plug with one end shaped like a strawberry fruit.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "When Barey decided in 2020 to pursue porn full-time, she did not imagine that at 28 she would spend more time hunched over a desk – not in the fun way – making flow charts, scheduling Zoom calls, and sending pitch decks. “I’m at my happiest when I’m making a video like putting a strawberry in my butt and pushing it out,” she says. “Now I’m on calls all day and I have tech neck.”", "reference": "2025 November 7, Alessandra Schade, quoting Stella Barey, “‘We’re sick of the OnlyFans model’: Stella Barey’s porn site lets gen Z sex workers have a life”, in The Guardian:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["earthberry", "strawb"], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "adjective", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈstɹɔːb(ə)ɹi/", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ʃt͡ʃɹɔːbɹi]", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈstɹɔˌbɛɹi/", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈstɹɑˌbɛɹi/", "tags": ["cot caught merger"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈstɹɒˌbɛɹi/", "tags": ["cot caught merger"]}], "forms": [{"word": "strawberrier", "tags": ["comparative"]}, {"word": "strawberriest", "tags": ["superlative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "Containing or having the flavor of strawberries.", "tags": [], "examples": ["I'd like a large strawberry shake."], "quotes": [{"text": "We sing you a song of the strawberriest Strawberry Ice Cream on earth.", "reference": "1941 May 8, Chicago Daily Tribune, volume C, number 110, page 8:"}, {"text": "At any rate, you will agree with me that this is the “strawberriest tastin’ ” pie that you’ve ever tasted.", "reference": "1948 May 5, St. Louis Post-Dispatch, volume 100, number 243, St. Louis, Mo., page 3D:"}, {"text": "Sixty seconds of boiling, and you’ll be admiring the strawberriest strawberry jam you ever tasted.", "reference": "1961 June, McCall’s, volume LXXXVIII, number 9, page 47:"}, {"text": "Fraser Recorded in Scotland in mid-1100s as de Frisselle, de Freseliere, de Fresel, as if from a place in France, and Sir Simon F— (executed 1306) is referred to as Simond Frysel; first element ?‘ash tree’ of, the –er ?to make it ‘strawberrier’ – a pun on the three silver cinquefoils or fraises in their armorials.", "reference": "1967, Basil Cottle, The Penguin Dictionary of Surnames, Penguin Books, published 1969, page 109:"}, {"text": "With at least 26 berries like these in every jar like this, how must Kraft Pure Strawberry Preserves taste? The strawberriest best!", "reference": "1968 March, Ladies’ Home Journal, volume LXXXV, Philadelphia, Pa.: The Curtis Publishing Company, page 122:"}, {"text": "And your strawberry ice cream can be the strawberriest and your peach ice cream the peachiest.", "reference": "1973, Glenn Andrews, Impromptu Cooking, New York, N.Y.: Atheneum, →ISBN, page 216:"}, {"text": "lessons exist because frozen strawberries in store are easier to pick but wild strawberries taste strawberrier.", "reference": "1975 fall, sue ellen farmer, The Student, page thirty-seven, column 2:"}, {"text": "My strawberriest of strawberry sauces was simply strawberries, whirred until chunky in the blender, then spooned over vanilla ice cream (or, in this case, low-fat ice milk).", "reference": "1978, Barbara [Halloran] Gibbons, The International Slim Gourmet Cookbook, Harper & Row, →ISBN, page 324:"}, {"text": "Now Jell-O® Strawberry Flavor Gelatin tastes even Strawberrier.", "reference": "1979 June 5, Family Circle, page 41:"}, {"text": "When used to sweeten out-of-season California strawberries, the berries are not only sweeter but “strawberrier,” with a flavor more like home-grown or field-ripened fruit.", "reference": "1982, Barbara [Halloran] Gibbons, Slim Gourmet Sweets and Treats, New York, N.Y.: Harper & Row, →ISBN, page 11:"}, {"text": "Kiwi, Kiwi, chirping bright / In the forests of the night / Only a Kiwi could be merrier / About shortcake so strawberrier!", "reference": "1998, Les Fox, Sue Fox, The Beanie Baby Handbook, West Highland Publishing Company, →ISBN, page 161:"}, {"text": "It occurred to me when I was last making the strawberries in dark syrup from How to Eat that there was no reason why I couldn’t use the balsamic vinegar – which provides the darkness and really does seem to make the strawberries strawberrier – when making jam.", "reference": "2000, Nigella Lawson, How to Be a Domestic Goddess: Baking and the Art of Comfort Cooking, London: Chatto & Windus, →ISBN, page 347:"}, {"text": "It’s the strawberriest shortcake ever.", "reference": "2004 May, Sunset, page 127:"}, {"text": "Down leaped Ron and milked the frothiest, fruitiest, strawberriest milkshake anybody had ever tasted.", "reference": "2005, Rowan Clifford, Rodeo Ron and His Milkshake Cows, Borzoi Books, →ISBN:"}, {"text": "“The strawberriest ice cream I have ever tasted!” was the verdict of my daughter Lindsay.", "reference": "2009, Annette Yates, Ice Cream Made Easy: Homemade Recipes for Ice Cream Machines, Right Way, →ISBN, page 39:"}, {"text": "Mind you, I have to admit they were three of the strawberriest looking strawberries I have ever seen.", "reference": "2011, Hartley Pool, Stranger in Taiwan, Revenge Ink, →ISBN, page 77:"}, {"text": "It was the strawberriest strawberry ever.", "reference": "2013, Caroline Green, Hold Your Breath, Piccadilly Press, →ISBN, page 125:"}, {"text": "HANNAH SAYS: “Wow, these are incredibly juicy. These are the strawberriest things in the world. They’re more strawberry[-]ish than actual strawberries. They’re incredible!”", "reference": "2013 January, Front, number 177, page 38:"}, {"text": "Right now, strawberries are their strawberriest.", "reference": "2022 June 9, Daniel Neman, “Strawberry spectacular”, in Hartford Courant, volume CLXXXVI, section 4, page 4, column 1:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Flavored with ethyl methylphenylglycidate, an artificial compound which is said to resemble the taste of strawberries.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Of a color similar to the color of strawberry-flavoured products.", "tags": [], "examples": ["The strawberry lipstick matched his outfit."], "quotes": [{"text": "They are, at once, beautiful and curious, with their translucent white skin and strawberriest blond hair, looking like a group of Wagner’s Valkyrie lost in a Puccini opera.", "reference": "2006, Ida Liberkowski, Cynthia Malizia, Along the Amalfi Drive, Lulu.com, →ISBN, page 282:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "jahodový"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "jordbær-"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "aardbeien-"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "mansikka-"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Erdbeer-"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "erdbeerig"}, {"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "苺味の"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "truskawkowy"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "de morango"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "земляни́чный"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "клубни́чный"}, {"language": {"code": "sk", "name": "Slovak"}, "word": "jahodový"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "jordgubbs-"}, {"language": {"code": "tr", "name": "Turkish"}, "word": "çilekli"}, {"language": {"code": "uk", "name": "Ukrainian"}, "word": "суни́чний"}, {"language": {"code": "uk", "name": "Ukrainian"},